ling or the emergence of clear nominees could shift the race, especially if Democrats sustain their 2026 special-election momentum into a high-turnout electorate.", "confidence": "low", "notes": ["No expert ratings published yet; forecast rests on fundamentals and polls.", "New or vacant seat with no expert ratings; fundamentals only.", "No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings."]}, "overview": "Florida remains a Republican-leaning state in presidential politics, and the open 2028 race starts with the GOP favored by about five points. Neither party has a settled nominee, and no general-election polls or expert ratings are available yet, leaving the forecast anchored to the state's underlying partisan lean.\n\nThere are some signs of Democratic life: the party posted strong results in 2026 special elections, and national figures like Pete Buttigieg have headlined Florida Democratic events. Still, special-election overperformance rarely translates fully to presidential turnout, and Republicans enter with a structural edge. The race is rated Lean Republican with wide uncertainty, and early polling or candidate developments could move it meaningfully in either direction.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.2832, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.3401, "margin": -4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.352, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.3574, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.3329, "margin": -4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.3466, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.3674, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.3674, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.3461, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.3181, "margin": -5.0}]}